# Rust Skills

This project bundles [rust-skills](https://github.com/leonardomso/rust-skills) at `.cursor/skills/rust-skills/`.

When working with Rust files:

1. Read `.cursor/skills/rust-skills/SKILL.md` first — it indexes 265 rules across 26 categories.
2. Open only the rule files relevant to the current task from `.cursor/skills/rust-skills/rules/`.
3. Prefer progressive disclosure: load `own-`, `err-`, and `mem-` rules for most changes; add `async-`, `unsafe-`, or `anti-` rules when the code touches those areas.
4. Apply the bad/good examples from matched rules before proposing changes.

Invoke explicitly with `/rust-skills` for reviews, e.g. `/rust-skills review this function`.
